  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">La r&#xe9;ponse d&#x2019;urgence aux besoins sanitaires critiques des populations affect&#xe9;es par les inondations au Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide lifesaving health assistance to over 280,000 people affected by the floods, ensuring and improving access to primary health services such as treatment of childhood illnesses, sexual and reproductive health, and maternal health. Overall, through this project WHO will ensure availability of health services by deploying mobile health clinics and medicines to assist affected people, will deploy a technical SURGE team to prevent outbreaks of water-borne diseases, and will make available emergency health kits. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 281,070 people, including 65,895 women and 153,688 children, and including as well 9,246 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
